From b884ee4e8e46165fe32d4084952ea4e604c30be5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:06:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tools: add arifi-sync - the currency, series and
 upstream-bump driver

Charter ask #2 ("make sure we actually get the latest versions of each, as they update
often") was prose, and it was silently not happening: remotes rocmfpx and powerinfer had
never been fetched at all, and a stale TurboQuant checkout caused a wall to be declared that
did not exist. This makes it code that fails.

  arifi_sync.py status | provenance | series regen/check/replay | currency | recipe | bump

Currency cannot be satisfied by doing nothing. It fails when a source has never been fetched,
when the last successful fetch is older than max_fetch_age_days, or when live head differs
from the reviewed pin. The only way to clear a drift row is to review the new commits and
write the sha you reviewed into sources.json - re-running the command cannot clear it.
state.json is gitignored on purpose: a clone inheriting our fetch timestamps would report
every source as fresh without ever fetching, which is the exact do-nothing pass this exists
to prevent.

The build recipe is recovered by DIFFING CMakeCache against a committed snapshot, never by
grepping it. Grepping for the flags you remember is how -D_WIN32_WINNT=0x0A00,
LLAMA_USE_PREBUILT_UI=OFF and -static-libgcc -static-libstdc++ were each missed, costing
three failed builds. The snapshot carries all 309 non-internal cache entries and exports a
CMake -C initial-cache file, so a replayed configure cannot omit a flag.

sources.json requires an explicit ref per source. PrismML's default branch is 'prism', not
main or master; resolving prisml/master silently reports a different branch's head as drift.
That mistake was made once while writing this tool.

F-085 binds: the regression judge is llama-server. judge refuses to start if sources.json
names anything else, and will not run a timed arm without an explicit bench-purity assertion.
bump refuses the bump unless replay AND build AND judge all pass.

Honest status, also recorded in the tool's README: status, provenance, series regen/check/
replay, currency and recipe are EXERCISED against this repository. build and judge are
written but UNEXERCISED - judge raises rather than returning a plausible-looking result,
because a procedure that is documented but never proven is the gap this slot exists to close.

Taken-from: ArifiLabs lane-110C fork-maintainability slot
Origin: ArifiLabs lane-110C
Measured-effect: tooling only; no engine behaviour changed. series check replays 38 patches to a byte-identical tree; currency fetched 4 remotes + 2 local checkouts and reported real drift.
